      "topic": "Etymology of achievement and hatchment",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The ancient term used in place of \"achievement\" was \"hatchment\", deriving (through such historic forms as atcheament, achement, hathement, etc.) from the French achèvement, from the French verb achever, a contraction of à chef venir (\"to come to a head\"), ultimately from Latin ad caput venire, \"to come to a head\", thus: \"to reach a conclusion, accomplish, achieve\"."
